Agricultural-Bot adaptation (2026-10-06/07):
- Bundle one plant with its meshes, textures, material and metadata.
- Use a local model://tomato_0 resource path rather than the upstream layout directory.
- Generate a deterministic 150-instance world with a solid ground collider.
- Package resources with ament_cmake and provide ROS 2 launch integration.

Plant fruit is part of the static visual mesh, not a detachable harvest object.

Random-fruit adaptation (2026-10-07):
- Derive tomato_plant from the original stem/leaf submeshes, retaining the same
  licensed mesh, textures, and upstream attribution without duplicating assets.
- Ground the derived asset's simplified stem collider (height 1.2416 m).
- Add separately generated static sphere targets and optional offline annotations.
- Keep tomato_0 and the non-randomized baseline unchanged.
Random targets do not yet implement attachment, detachment, or harvest physics.

Single-fruit mesh adaptation (2026-10-07):
- Extract one connected body (component index 2) of Fruit1 from the bundled
  tomato_0 COLLADA instead of placing an entire multi-fruit cluster.
- Preserve original UV coordinates and vertex normals, center the body, and
  uniformly normalize it into a bounding sphere of radius 0.5.
- Keep the original ripe AG15frt1.png and unripe AG15frt4.png textures in tomato_0.
- Record source component, normalization and SHA-256 hashes in
  models/tomato_fruit/SOURCE.json; retain Apache-2.0 license and attribution.
- Provide scripts/extract_tomato_fruit.py to reproduce the derived asset using
  the Python standard library. Original assets are not rewritten.
